.\" Manual page for launcher-rs.
.\" Keep the OPTIONS section in sync with `launcher-rs --help`
.\" (tests/cli.rs checks that every long flag is documented here).
.TH LAUNCHER-RS 1 "2026-11-27" "launcher-rs 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
launcher-rs \- dmenu-style application launcher strip with icons for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launcher-rs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.IB command " | launcher-rs \-\-dmenu"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B launcher-rs
shows a horizontal strip at the edge of a monitor with the installed
applications (XDG
.I .desktop
entries) and their icons.
Typing filters the list incrementally; pressing
.B Enter
launches the selected application.
.PP
It talks to the X server directly and renders in software, without a GUI
toolkit.
The strip is an override-redirect window: it has no borders and does not
steal focus from the window manager.
Only one instance runs per display; starting it again while it is open does
nothing.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-dmenu ,
items are read from standard input, one per line, and the selected line is
printed to standard output, like
.BR dmenu (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Command line options override the configuration file.
Values may be given as a separate argument or inline
.RB ( \-\-height=24 ).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Read the configuration from
.IR FILE ,
which must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Use the built-in color theme
.IR NAME ,
overriding the theme from the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-themes
List the built-in themes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt " \fITEXT\fR"
Prompt text shown before the input field (default
.RB \(dq Run:\ \(dq ;
empty with
.BR \-\-dmenu ).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bottom
Place the strip at the bottom edge of the monitor.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edge " \fBtop\fR|\fBbottom\fR"
Monitor edge to attach the strip to.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monitor " \fITARGET\fR"
Monitor to use:
.B focused
(the monitor with the active window; default),
.BR primary ,
.B pointer
(or
.BR mouse ),
a RandR monitor index
.RB ( 0 ", " 1 ", ...)"
or a connector name such as
.BR HDMI\-A\-0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-height " PX"
Strip height in pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-margin " PX"
Outer horizontal margin in pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " PX"
Distance from the monitor edge in pixels, e.g. the height of a status bar.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " \fIPX\fR|\fIPERCENT\fB%\fR"
Strip width in pixels or as a percentage of the monitor width.
.TP
.BR \-\-align " \fBleft\fR|\fBcenter\fR|\fBright\fR"
Horizontal alignment when the strip is narrower than the monitor.
.TP
.BR \-fn ", " \-\-font " \fIFAMILY\fR"
Font family.
Generic names such as
.BR Sans ,
.B Serif
and
.B Monospace
are accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-size " PX"
Font size in pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon\-size " PX"
Icon size in pixels (default 24).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-icons
Do not draw icons.
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal " CMD"
Terminal used for entries with
.BR Terminal=true .
.TP
.B \-\-case\-sensitive
Make the search case-sensitive.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Make the search case-insensitive (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-match " \fBprefix\fR|\fBsubstring\fR|\fBfuzzy\fR"
Matching strategy.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dmenu
Read items from standard input and print the selection.
.TP
.B \-\-exec
With
.BR \-\-dmenu ,
run the selected line through the configured shell instead of printing it.
.TP
.B \-\-print
Print the selected application instead of launching it.
.TP
.BR \-nb ", " \-\-normal\-bg " \fICOLOR\fR"
Background color.
.TP
.BR \-nf ", " \-\-normal\-fg " \fICOLOR\fR"
Text color.
.TP
.BR \-sb ", " \-\-selected\-bg " \fICOLOR\fR"
Background color of the selected item.
.TP
.BR \-sf ", " \-\-selected\-fg " \fICOLOR\fR"
Text color of the selected item.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
Colors are written as
.BR #rgb ,
.BR #rrggbb ,
.B #rrggbbaa
or one of
.BR black ,
.B white
and
.BR transparent .
.PP
For
.BR dmenu (1)
compatibility,
.B \-f
is accepted and ignored, and
.BR \-l / \-\-lines " and " \-w / \-\-embed
are accepted with a warning but not implemented.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Run the selected item.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch between applications and the executables found in
.BR $PATH .
No effect with
.BR \-\-dmenu .
.TP
.B Escape
Close without running anything.
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " Ctrl+P / Ctrl+N
Move the selection.
.TP
.BR Left / Right
Move the selection.
.TP
.BR Page\ Up / Page\ Down
Move the selection by 10 items.
.TP
.BR Home / End ", " Ctrl+A / Ctrl+E
Move the text cursor to the start or end; pressed again, select the first or
last item.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+B / Ctrl+F
Move the text cursor by one character.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right ", " Alt+B / Alt+F
Move the text cursor by one word.
.TP
.BR Backspace / Delete ", " Ctrl+H / Ctrl+D
Delete one character.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+W ", " Ctrl+U ", " Ctrl+K
Delete the previous word, everything before the cursor, or everything after
it.
.PP
Clicking an item selects it; the mouse wheel moves the selection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
An item was launched or printed, or another instance was already running.
.TP
.B 1
Closed without a selection.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, configuration or another error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_CONFIG
Configuration file to use when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the configuration file.
.TP
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_DIRS
Directories searched for applications and icon themes.
.TP
.B PATH
Executables listed after pressing
.BR Tab ,
and the search path for
.B TryExec
and
.BR Exec .
.TP
.B TERMINAL
Terminal used for
.B Terminal=true
entries when none is configured.
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_DEBUG
When set, print timings and diagnostics to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/launcher\-rs/config.toml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/launcher\-rs/config.toml
Configuration file; the first existing one is used.
Unknown keys are rejected.
See
.I config.example.toml
in the source distribution for every option.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk\-3.0/settings.ini
.TQ
.I ~/.config/gtk\-4.0/settings.ini
The icon theme is taken from
.B gtk\-icon\-theme\-name
when none is configured.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B launcher\-rs \-b \-\-theme tokyo\-night
Strip at the bottom of the focused monitor with a built-in theme.
.TP
.B launcher\-rs \-\-width 60% \-\-align center \-\-offset 24
Centered strip, 60% wide, below a 24 pixel status bar.
.TP
.B printf \(aqone\entwo\en\(aq | launcher\-rs \-\-dmenu \-p \(aqChoose: \(aq
Pick a line from standard input.
.TP
.B ls | launcher\-rs \-\-dmenu \-\-exec
Run the selected line through the shell.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR rofi (1)
.PP
https://github.com/EitaPreulaJhol/launcher-rs
